## Incident Classification

### Severity Levels

| Level | Definition | Example |
|-------|------------|---------|
| Level 1 | Complete business disruption | Data center loss, ransomware |
| Level 2 | Major disruption, partial operations | Region failure, critical system down |
| Level 3 | Significant impact, workarounds available | Single service failure |
| Level 4 | Minor impact, limited scope | Non-critical system issue |

### Trigger Events

| Event Type | Severity | Response |
|------------|----------|----------|
| Natural Disaster | 1-2 | Full BCP activation |
| Cyber Attack | 1-2 | IR + BCP activation |
| Cloud Provider Outage | 2-3 | Failover procedures |
| Power Outage | 2-4 | Remote work + cloud ops |
| Pandemic | 2 | Remote operations |
| Office Inaccessible | 3 | Remote work |
| Key Personnel Loss | 3-4 | Succession procedures |

